 { Here is a more complex endgame, which features a similar restriction technique. Thanks to Black's passive king, White has real chances of obtaining two far advanced passed pawns on the kingside. But how should that plan be initiated? } 1. { -KEY- } h5 $2 { We will soon see the defect of this move. } ( { a) } 1. Kg6 $2 { was also bad in view of } Be1 ) 
