 { Despite a symmetrical pawn structure, White has some advantage here thanks to his more active pieces. } 1. { -KEY- } Ba6 $1 ( { Preventing } 1. Ba6 Rc8 ) 
Re8 $2 { Too passive. } ( { Black should have tried } 1... Bd5 { in order to liberate himself by ...Ne4-c5 and ...f7-f6, although after } 2. f3 $1 Bxa2 3. Ra1 Bb3 ( { or } 3... Bd5 4. e4 ) 
4. Ra3 Bc2 5. Nc6 Nd5 6. e4 Ne7 7. Bb7 Re8 8. Nd4 { followed by Rxa7, White is still better - Kharitonov. } ) 
2. f3 $1 { With this and his next move, White prevents the enemy plan outlined in the previous note. } Ba8 ( { Or } 2... Bd5 3. b3 { followed by e3-e4 with similar play - Kharitonov. } ) 
3. e4 Ke7 4. Kf2 g5 { Unfortunately for Black, the knight can't move either here or later due to Rd7+, while ...Rd8 obviously leads to the loss of the f7-pawn. Thus he is left without a constructive plan, and his position can be considered as lost already. } 5. Ke3 Rf8 6. b4 $1 { With the powerful idea of b4-b5 and Nc6+. } Rb8 ( { A tactical try with } 6... b5 7. Bxb5 Rb8 { fails to } 8. Bc6 $1 { - Kharitonov. } ) 
7. b5 Re8 ( { Perhaps Pigusov only realized at this point that } 7... Bb7 { fails to } 8. Nc6 Bxc6 9. bxc6 Ne8 10. Rd7 Kf6 11. c7 { etc. } ) 
8. Nc6+ Kf8 ( { After } 8... Bxc6 9. bxc6 { the c-pawn decides - Kharitonov. } ) 
9. Nxa7 ( { In view of } 10. Nc8 { next, Black resigned. } ) 

