 { An extreme form of restriction occurs when a piece, typically a rook, is imprisoned by the enemy forces, thus losing its normal functionality. Here are a few cases of such isolation.With two sound extra pawns White is winning. Black's last move, ...b7-b6, motivated me to play for a little trick. } 1. { -KEY- } Rf1+ $1 Ke7 ( { Objectively } 1... Kg5 { was better, when } 2. Ke3 { preparing Rd1-d4, is just one idea. } ) 
2. Rf5 Kd6 3. Rxe5 $1 Kxe5 4. Bc4 { Material is now even, but Black's rook is no longer a normal rook, of course. } Kd4 5. g4 ( { In view of } 5. g4 Rxc4 ( { or } 5. g4 Ke4 6. g5 Kf5 7. Kd2 Kxg5 8. Kc3 ) 
6. bxc4 Kxc4 7. g5 Kd5 8. Kd3 { Black resigned. } ) 

 1-0

