 { In this innocent-looking position White found a way to apply the idea of isolation. } 1. { -KEY- } Bxc5 $1 Rxc5 2. c4 { Suddenly the rook on c5 is short of breathing space. } Re8 3. f4 a5 { Obviously, the threat of b2-b4 had to parried. } ( { If } 3... Ra5 { then } 4. g4 $1 Be6 ( { or } 4... Bg6 5. b4 $1 Ra4 6. f5 { with material gains } ) 
5. a4 c5 6. b3 $1 { with a decisive advantage - Adorjan. In effect, Black is a rook down here. } ) 
4. g4 $1 Bg6 5. h4 { Gaining more space. } ( { In contrast, after } 5. Nxg6 $6 Rxe1 6. Rxe1 hxg6 7. b3 b5 { Black might soon be able to liberate his rook, with increased chances of survival. } ) 
Rd8 ( { Or } 5... Rexe5 6. Rxe5 Rxc4 7. Rf1 { and White's kingside initiative should take its toll. } ) 
6. b3 b5 ( { The optimistic } 6... Rd2 { fails to the simple } 7. Rad1 $1 { intending } Rxa2 8. Nxg6 hxg6 9. Re8 ) 
7. h5 Be8 ( { On } 7... Bd3 { Adorjan had prepared } 8. Rad1 bxc4 9. bxc4 Bc2 ( { or } 9... Bxc4 10. Rxd8 Kxd8 11. Rc1 ) 
10. Rxd8 Kxd8 11. Rc1 { with inevitable material losses for Black; e.g. } Be4 12. Kf2 $1 a4 13. Ke3 Bg2 14. Rg1 Bh3 15. Kd4 Ra5 16. Nxc6 ) 
8. a4 $1 { Very nice, ruling out any attempts at ...d5xc4 followed by ...a5-a4 and ...Ra5. By now the rook on c5 resembles a statue. } bxc4 9. bxc4 Rd4 10. Kh2 $1 g6 ( { Or } 10... Rxf4 11. Nd3 { with decisive material gains - Adorjan. } ) 
11. hxg6 hxg6 12. Rad1 ( { Black resigned, in view of } 12. Rad1 Rxe5 ( { or } 12. Rad1 Rxd1 13. Rxd1 g5 14. Kg3 $1 ) 
13. fxe5 Rxc4 14. e6 Rc5 15. Rd2 Rd5 16. Red1 { - Adorjan. } ) 

